  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for the Implementation of the Argentine Fund for International Cooperation (FO.AR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to contribute to the development of international cooperation in the implementation of the Argentine Fund for International Cooperation (FO.AR). For this, IOM will cooperate with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, International Trade and Worship (MRECIC), by providing technical support services for the mobility of experts and the implementation of operational activities, in accordance with the standards of the MRECIC and the IOM. The project will contribute to the economic and social development of the Argentine Republic, as well as other States of the Global South, through the implementation of programs linked to migration, supporting practical measures at the regional, national and local levels. The project will support the mobility of experts in the framework of international cooperation actions that would benefit societies of the beneficiary countries and the migrant population in them. It will also contribute across the board to achieve the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) of the 2030 Agenda, especially SDG 10: Reduce inequality in and between countries and SDG 17: Revitalize the Global Partnership for Sustainable Development.</narrative>
  </description>
